  "question": {
    "text": "The primary side of a transformer is connected to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>230</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> supply. The turn ratio of primary to secondary winding is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Load resistance connected to the secondary side is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>46</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>. The power consumed in it is:",
