  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The voltages associated with the primary and the secondary side of the transformer are related to the turn ratio as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo> </mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo> </mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>230</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>23</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the power consumed can be calculated as follows</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>P</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>23</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow><mn>46</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> </p>",
    "image": null
  },
